## **Phase 3: ESP32 Programming** 💻

### **Step 10: Write Arduino Code**

Create a new sketch with this code:

```cpp
#include <WiFi.h>
#include <FirebaseESP32.h>
#include "DHT.h"

#define DHTPIN 4
#define DHTTYPE DHT11

DHT dht(DHTPIN, DHTTYPE);

// Replace with your credentials
#define DATABASE_URL "https://esp32-dht-project-xxxxx.firebaseio.com/"
#define DATABASE_SECRET "your_database_secret_here"

const char* ssid = "your_wifi_name";
const char* password = "your_wifi_password";

FirebaseData firebaseData;
FirebaseAuth auth;
FirebaseConfig config;

void setup() {
  Serial.begin(115200);
  dht.begin();

  WiFi.begin(ssid, password);
  Serial.print("Connecting to WiFi");
  
  while (WiFi.status() != WL_CONNECTED) {
    Serial.print(".");
    delay(300);
  }
  
  Serial.println("\nWiFi Connected!");
  Serial.print("IP: ");
  Serial.println(WiFi.localIP());

  config.database_url = DATABASE_URL;
  config.signer.tokens.legacy_token = DATABASE_SECRET;

  Firebase.begin(&config, &auth);
  Firebase.reconnectWiFi(true);

  Serial.println("Firebase Initialized!");
}

void loop() {
  float h = dht.readHumidity();
  float t = dht.readTemperature();

  if (isnan(h) || isnan(t)) {
    Serial.println("Failed to read sensor!");
    delay(3000);
    return;
  }

  Serial.printf("Temp: %.1f°C  Humidity: %.1f%%\n", t, h);

  if (Firebase.setFloat(firebaseData, "/sensor/temperature", t)) {
    Serial.println("✓ Temperature uploaded");
  } else {
    Serial.println("✗ Error: " + firebaseData.errorReason());
  }

  if (Firebase.setFloat(firebaseData, "/sensor/humidity", h)) {
    Serial.println("✓ Humidity uploaded");
  } else {
    Serial.println("✗ Error: " + firebaseData.errorReason());
  }

  Serial.println("---");
  delay(3000);
}
```

### **Step 11: Configure Arduino IDE**
1. **Tools → Board** → Select your ESP32 board (e.g., "ESP32 Dev Module")
2. **Tools → Port** → Select COM port where ESP32 is connected
3. **Tools → Upload Speed** → 115200

### **Step 12: Upload Code**
1. Click **Upload** button (→)
2. Wait for "Done uploading"
3. Open **Serial Monitor** (Tools → Serial Monitor)
4. Set baud rate to **115200**

### **Step 13: Verify Data Upload**
Check Serial Monitor output:
```
WiFi Connected!
IP: 192.168.1.100
Firebase Initialized!
Temp: 25.5°C  Humidity: 62.6%
✓ Temperature uploaded
✓ Humidity uploaded
---
```

### **Step 14: Check Firebase Console**
1. Go to Firebase Console → Realtime Database → Data tab
2. You should see:
   ```
   sensor
     ├── temperature: 25.5
     └── humidity: 62.6
   ```

